; TUTORIAL.SCR — items for the new player tutorial at the gates of Fayd
; =====================================================================
; Sergeant Aldren Fairweather, who walks new characters through the basic
; commands in room 201 (Main Street, Gatehouse), is built into the engine
; (engine/internal/engine/tutorial.go), not scripted. This file holds only the
; object his lesson uses.
;
; ID ranges (the 95xx block is reserved for the tutorial):
;   INUMBER 9500
; =====================================================================

; ── The tutorial coin ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
; Placed in room 201 when the lesson reaches GET COIN ("a tarnished copper
; coin": ADJ1=318 tarnished, ADJ2=68 copper). Real coins go straight into the
; purse (currency.go), so this is a plain MISC item the player can GET,
; EXAMINE and DROP like anything else. It's worth nothing.
INUMBER 9500
NAME 229
MISC
WEIGHT 1
VOLUME 1
SUBSTANCE SOFTMETAL
*DESCRIPTION_START EXAMINE
A thin copper coin, worn nearly smooth by countless hands. The face stamped on one side is too rubbed away to recognize, and a tiny notch has been filed into its edge, the way the gate watch marks the coins they use for teaching newcomers.
*DESCRIPTION_END
;
